WEBVTT

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:04.530
The next stop is Tabata. Tabata.

00:03:05.870 --> 00:03:10.460
Transfer here for the Yamanote Line
bound for Ikebukuro, Shinjuku, and Shibuya.

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:13.290
We will soon be stopping in Tabata.

00:03:13.290 --> 00:03:15.460
The doors will open on the right side.

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:18.340
Good morning, Takayama.

00:03:18.340 --> 00:03:19.800
How'd you know it was me?

00:03:19.800 --> 00:03:22.470
I recognized the sound of your footsteps.

00:03:23.930 --> 00:03:26.470
You don't believe me, do you?

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:29.730
Sasshou, are you starting OJT this week?

00:03:29.730 --> 00:03:33.150
At Japan Foods Inc., yeah.

00:03:33.150 --> 00:03:34.730
You gonna show me the ropes, boss?

00:03:34.730 --> 00:03:37.940
"Boss"? We're the same age.

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:40.320
You took the OJT before me, right?

00:03:40.320 --> 00:03:42.360
By a month.

00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:45.700
It feels like I've worked a year, though.

00:03:45.700 --> 00:03:47.790
The PSF seems really tough.

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:48.580
It is.

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:53.830
Maybe I should've applied for
an attendant job like you, Sasshou.

00:03:53.830 --> 00:03:55.210
Oh, you.

00:03:56.540 --> 00:03:59.340
We have arrived in Tabata.

00:03:59.340 --> 00:04:00.590
Oh!

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:07.890
The Yamanote Line has also arrived. Once again, we are in Tabata.

00:04:07.890 --> 00:04:11.520
What a great sound. That's the 231 series, right?

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:12.600
Yep!

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:15.190
Wanna go again?

00:04:15.190 --> 00:04:17.110
Don't we always?

00:04:29.740 --> 00:04:32.960
I think the 231 series will win.

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:35.420
No way, this one's winning.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:37.790
Then the bets are placed.

00:04:44.340 --> 00:04:48.010
Those on tracks 5 and 6, please step back.

00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:51.680
The Yamanote Line and
Keihin-Tohoku Line have arrived.

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:55.060
We are now at Tokyo Station.

00:04:55.060 --> 00:04:56.770
Damn it, why?

00:04:56.770 --> 00:05:00.020
The 231 series seemed in better shape today.

00:05:00.020 --> 00:05:00.980
Seriously?

00:05:01.650 --> 00:05:04.490
You have much to learn, grasshopper.

00:05:04.490 --> 00:05:06.990
Well, I'm this way. Later!

00:05:06.990 --> 00:05:08.780
Yeah, later!

00:05:12.290 --> 00:05:14.330
Enemy of women!

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:16.790
Give up!

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:18.080
Her?

00:05:19.250 --> 00:05:21.460
What are you doing, Sakurai?

00:05:21.460 --> 00:05:22.710
I caught a criminal!

00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:25.220
Come on. What exactly did he do?

00:05:25.630 --> 00:05:27.050
He's out cold!

00:05:27.050 --> 00:05:29.550
Your pity is wasted on the evil.

00:05:29.550 --> 00:05:32.970
Look, that's not what I'm talking about...

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:35.890
Excuse me.

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:36.690
Huh?!

00:05:36.690 --> 00:05:38.480
Uh, um...

00:05:38.850 --> 00:05:40.230
WhatвЂ”

00:05:41.150 --> 00:05:43.320
How can I take the bullet train?

00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:46.320
Is there anything special I have to do?

00:05:46.320 --> 00:05:50.830
Uh, he just said "bullet train", right?

00:05:50.830 --> 00:05:51.950
Right?

00:05:54.750 --> 00:05:59.460
To take the bullet train, you need a
limited express ticket and a normal one.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:04.630
If you need some help,
there is a ticket office over there.

00:06:04.630 --> 00:06:05.420
Thank you!

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:08.180
Thank you, Koumi.

00:06:09.220 --> 00:06:12.220
Seriously, at least learn <i>some</i> English.

00:06:12.220 --> 00:06:16.020
Railway stuff takes up too much of my brain.
English just doesn't stick.

00:06:31.320 --> 00:06:33.450
There is no God!

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:37.870
Why do I have to write an apology for taking down a criminal?

00:06:37.870 --> 00:06:41.000
And make sure to use a pen, not a pencil.

00:06:42.460 --> 00:06:44.340
I have to rewrite this?

00:06:44.340 --> 00:06:45.050
Here.

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:51.300
Thanks.

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:55.850
This sucks.

00:06:56.350 --> 00:07:00.230
Why do I have to be so damn detailed?

00:07:01.150 --> 00:07:02.020
Sakurai.

00:07:04.270 --> 00:07:05.980
I'll help. Give it here.

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:08.240
I'm fine.

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:10.910
No man's gonna get the better of me.

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:12.910
What the heck?

00:07:12.910 --> 00:07:16.450
Still, why'd you knock him out?

00:07:16.450 --> 00:07:18.410
You could've just restrained him.

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:21.870
It's simpler to take them out that way.

00:07:21.870 --> 00:07:24.340
It's not so simple now, though, is it?

00:07:25.670 --> 00:07:27.340
This time's an exception.

00:07:27.710 --> 00:07:32.220
Aoi, is there anything I can help with?

00:07:32.220 --> 00:07:34.680
Thanks, but I'm fine.

00:07:34.680 --> 00:07:36.220
I can finish this myself.

00:07:36.220 --> 00:07:38.060
You spelled that word wrong.

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:38.680
What?

00:07:38.680 --> 00:07:40.480
Third line. It's "your", not "you're".

00:07:40.480 --> 00:07:42.230
Man, I'm hungry.

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:47.570
What's this supposed to be?

00:07:47.570 --> 00:07:50.240
I can't imagine what it looks like from reading the name.

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:52.360
It's fish.

00:07:52.360 --> 00:07:56.700
The texture is such that you might even think it's land meat.

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:58.370
Oh?

00:07:58.370 --> 00:07:59.950
Then what about this?

00:07:59.950 --> 00:08:02.080
Broad bean soup, huh?

00:08:02.080 --> 00:08:04.750
That's quite a popular dish in the Mediterranean.

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:08.960
The Mediterranean, huh? I've always wanted to take the Trans-Siberian Railway there.

00:08:08.960 --> 00:08:12.840
I doubt that runs all the way to the Mediterranean.

00:08:12.840 --> 00:08:15.930
More importantly, what are you two doing here?

00:08:15.930 --> 00:08:19.520
We wanted to try this place. Yeah?

00:08:20.060 --> 00:08:21.270
M-Meuni...

00:08:21.270 --> 00:08:23.190
Great teamwork.

00:08:23.190 --> 00:08:24.190
You think so?

00:08:24.190 --> 00:08:26.150
That wasn't a compliment, stupid.

00:08:26.150 --> 00:08:27.730
Then what <i>were</i> you saying?

00:08:27.730 --> 00:08:31.490
That you don't belong in this restaurant, Takayama!

00:08:33.200 --> 00:08:35.660
A-And what, you do, Sakurai?

00:08:37.910 --> 00:08:40.660
Aoi, have you decided
what you're going to order?

00:08:41.080 --> 00:08:44.040
I recommend the chef's lunch special.

00:08:44.870 --> 00:08:45.790
Sasshou?

00:08:45.790 --> 00:08:46.380
Bleu...

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:48.040
Welcome, Takayama.

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:52.340
Your OJT is here, Sasshou?

00:08:55.180 --> 00:08:58.050
Well? Does this uniform look good on me?

00:08:58.510 --> 00:08:59.560
Yeah.

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:02.890
"Yeah"? That's it?

00:09:02.890 --> 00:09:03.980
Um...

00:09:03.980 --> 00:09:07.770
Oh, I'm Mari Sasshou. I'm in
11th grade at Kiryuu Rail High.

00:09:07.770 --> 00:09:10.230
I hope Takayama hasn't
caused you any trouble.

00:09:10.230 --> 00:09:13.740
Oh, no. On the contrary.

00:09:13.740 --> 00:09:15.610
You look like a doll.

00:09:15.610 --> 00:09:18.450
That uniform looks great on you.

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:22.950
You go to the same rail high school? You must love trains, then.

00:09:22.950 --> 00:09:24.080
Huh?

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:25.460
Oh, yes.

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:29.880
She enjoys things like the sounds of trains and station departure bells. Right?

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:30.920
Yes.

00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:33.170
A train sound remixer?

00:09:33.170 --> 00:09:37.050
Are rail high schools filled
with people like Takayama?

00:09:37.050 --> 00:09:40.350
Not everyone can be as weird as Takayama.

00:09:48.020 --> 00:09:50.610
Excuse me. One taiyaki, please.

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:52.610
Takayama?

00:09:59.570 --> 00:10:01.200
Seat back, check!

00:10:01.200 --> 00:10:02.830
Seat, check!

00:10:03.330 --> 00:10:05.540
All right! It's okay to sit.

00:10:06.830 --> 00:10:09.830
You don't have to worry about a little dirt.

00:10:11.000 --> 00:10:13.670
You did that before, remember?

00:10:13.670 --> 00:10:14.880
Did I?

00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:18.430
It was when we first started school.
You really surprised me.

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:21.430
Desk, check! Chair, check!

00:10:21.430 --> 00:10:24.140
Right in the middle of the class!

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:26.930
Point-and-check confirmation is
a basic part of a train driver's job.

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:31.900
Everyone burst out laughing, but I was really impressed.

00:10:32.520 --> 00:10:35.820
I realized just how serious you were about becoming a train driver.

00:10:43.120 --> 00:10:46.410
What's gonna happen to me, you think?

00:10:47.160 --> 00:10:50.540
Can I make it in the Public Security Force?

00:10:54.250 --> 00:10:56.670
What will be, will be, I guess.

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:05.680
Um, that girl's name was Sakurai, right?

00:11:06.470 --> 00:11:09.730
I think people like her are suited to the Public Safety Force.

00:11:09.730 --> 00:11:10.900
You think so?

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:14.820
With only people like her,
peace might actually take a dive.

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:17.820
We'd be prisoners on the rails.

00:11:17.820 --> 00:11:20.030
Honestly, who even knows
what's going on in that brain of hers?

00:11:22.740 --> 00:11:24.830
Ms. Iida isn't here, huh?

00:11:27.830 --> 00:11:29.330
The diesel engine in my head is keeping me from working!

00:11:29.330 --> 00:11:30.290
Thanks.

00:11:30.290 --> 00:11:31.540
The diesel engine in my head is keeping me from working!

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:35.040
This is a summary table of
today's lost-and-found items.

00:11:35.040 --> 00:11:36.460
Put it there, please.

00:11:36.460 --> 00:11:37.340
Okay.

00:11:38.710 --> 00:11:40.930
Need any help?

00:11:41.300 --> 00:11:43.260
Yes, please, Koumi!

00:11:43.260 --> 00:11:44.890
Not a problem.

00:11:47.890 --> 00:11:49.600
Click here.

00:11:49.600 --> 00:11:50.350
Huh?

00:11:50.350 --> 00:11:52.560
O-Oh. Here, huh?

00:11:52.560 --> 00:11:54.860
Then click here.

00:11:57.320 --> 00:11:58.820
C-Click.

00:12:05.200 --> 00:12:06.450
Ow.

00:12:13.710 --> 00:12:15.040
A missing person?

00:12:15.040 --> 00:12:21.010
My friend, Kaori.
We made ringtones together.

00:12:21.470 --> 00:12:24.050
But she's been gone since last night.

00:12:25.340 --> 00:12:29.350
She went to record sounds at some station,
and that's the last I heard from her.

00:12:30.100 --> 00:12:33.020
I called her over and over,
but she never answered.

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:36.360
Do you know which station she went to?

00:12:36.360 --> 00:12:37.400
No idea.

00:12:38.980 --> 00:12:41.530
You think she went on a trip after?

00:12:42.740 --> 00:12:45.740
She'd still pick up the phone
if that were the case.

00:12:48.120 --> 00:12:49.280
Don't worry.

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:54.210
We'll find your friend Kaori.

00:12:54.210 --> 00:12:55.750
Takayama!

00:12:56.500 --> 00:12:58.250
It'll be fine.

00:12:58.250 --> 00:12:59.800
We got this covered!

00:13:03.510 --> 00:13:06.890
These are all the reports from yesterday.

00:13:06.890 --> 00:13:11.770
If she got into some kind of trouble anywhere
in Tokyo, there should be some info on it here.

00:13:36.120 --> 00:13:37.460
Listen, people!

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:40.630
This group is known for their radical plans!

00:13:40.630 --> 00:13:42.550
Do not let down your guards!

00:13:42.550 --> 00:13:43.460
Sir!

00:13:43.460 --> 00:13:45.970
PSF Riot Police, move out!

00:13:45.970 --> 00:13:46.510
Yeah!

00:13:51.970 --> 00:13:54.310
Like a pack of wolves as always.

00:13:55.980 --> 00:13:57.440
Did you figure anything out?

00:13:57.980 --> 00:14:00.560
Not yet.

00:14:00.560 --> 00:14:03.690
If we just had some clue...

00:14:04.320 --> 00:14:07.110
Should I ask the other squads for help?

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:18.960
We'll keep at it a little longer.

00:14:20.960 --> 00:14:22.670
I see, I see.

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:25.260
Good!

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:31.680
I'm going to the restroom.

00:14:35.970 --> 00:14:37.140
Takayama!

00:14:37.730 --> 00:14:40.060
I'm sorry for all the trouble this must be.

00:14:40.060 --> 00:14:41.650
Don't worry about it.

00:14:41.650 --> 00:14:45.440
Helping people in need
is our job as members of the PSF.

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:49.450
I'm impressed.

00:14:49.450 --> 00:14:51.450
Huh? With what?

00:14:52.030 --> 00:14:54.870
There were these people from the PSF
that left just a little earlier.

00:14:56.450 --> 00:14:59.250
I realized how tough the job must be.

00:15:00.170 --> 00:15:03.250
They're kind of a special case.

00:15:03.250 --> 00:15:06.090
Takayama, is that what your job's like?

00:15:06.090 --> 00:15:08.760
Uh, sometimes.

00:15:10.090 --> 00:15:11.550
Takayama!

00:15:11.550 --> 00:15:13.220
Yes?

00:15:13.220 --> 00:15:15.930
I had a question for you.

00:15:15.930 --> 00:15:17.600
Okay.

00:15:17.600 --> 00:15:19.270
Well, see you later.

00:15:24.020 --> 00:15:24.980
Huh?

00:15:25.320 --> 00:15:27.280
That ringtone...

00:15:27.280 --> 00:15:28.110
Huh?

00:15:31.450 --> 00:15:34.200
This is Kaori's. I'm sure of it!

00:15:34.200 --> 00:15:35.910
Where was this cellphone found?

00:15:35.910 --> 00:15:40.790
Someone dropped it off after they found their child playing with it.

00:15:40.790 --> 00:15:43.670
They couldn't tell us where
they had picked it up, though.

00:15:44.460 --> 00:15:45.710
No way.

00:15:47.130 --> 00:15:48.800
Are there any pictures we can go off of?

00:15:50.010 --> 00:15:51.760
What's in her recent calls?

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:54.390
We finally have a lead.

00:15:54.390 --> 00:15:56.220
Please, give us something that helps.

00:15:58.930 --> 00:16:00.270
What about audio files?

00:16:01.940 --> 00:16:04.270
Knowing Kaori, she might have
left something behind.

00:16:05.150 --> 00:16:06.190
Koumi!

00:16:06.190 --> 00:16:08.570
This is the last recording.

00:16:10.740 --> 00:16:11.900
I'm playing it now.

00:16:12.740 --> 00:16:14.660
What do you think you're doing, bitch?

00:16:14.660 --> 00:16:15.990
Let me go!

00:16:15.990 --> 00:16:17.660
Shut your mouth! Come here!

00:16:20.620 --> 00:16:24.330
Do we have an incident

00:16:24.670 --> 00:16:26.290
on our hands?

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:28.420
Kaori.

00:16:28.420 --> 00:16:29.460
What do we do?
Kaori.

00:16:29.460 --> 00:16:30.800
Seriously, what?

00:16:32.300 --> 00:16:36.550
Koumi, is there anything else on that sound file?

00:16:37.300 --> 00:16:38.810
It looks like that's it.

00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:40.100
Damn it!

00:16:40.600 --> 00:16:42.560
That doesn't help us at all.

00:16:43.020 --> 00:16:44.140
What do we do?

00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:46.980
Sasshou?

00:16:56.740 --> 00:17:00.490
Can't you tell what station
it was left at by smelling it?

00:17:00.490 --> 00:17:01.620
How the hell could I?

00:17:01.620 --> 00:17:03.410
You're obsessed with trains, aren't you?

00:17:03.410 --> 00:17:06.250
The least you could do is pick up
a useful skill from your obsession!

00:17:32.230 --> 00:17:33.440
I think...

00:17:35.450 --> 00:17:38.450
Sasshou, did you figure something out?

00:17:39.160 --> 00:17:39.910
Yeah.

00:17:47.870 --> 00:17:49.630
Is this really it?

00:17:50.460 --> 00:17:52.920
Why are we right by the ocean?

00:17:53.460 --> 00:17:56.380
Umi-Shibaura Station on the JNR Tsurumi Line.

00:17:57.510 --> 00:18:00.970
Its station platform faces the
Keihin Canal, which is rather rare.

00:18:01.310 --> 00:18:02.970
But why here?

00:18:02.970 --> 00:18:07.980
It was faint, but I could hear the sound of waves against a wall on that sound file.

00:18:12.270 --> 00:18:15.280
I also heard the sound of a brake test.

00:18:15.280 --> 00:18:18.280
They only do that at return stations.

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:20.030
You mean...

00:18:20.030 --> 00:18:21.280
Yes.

00:18:21.280 --> 00:18:28.750
The only JNR station nearby where one could record these sounds would be Umi-Shibaura.

00:18:29.670 --> 00:18:31.750
She heard the waves, huh?

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:34.250
Sasshou's ears are never wrong.

00:18:34.710 --> 00:18:37.340
This is where Kaori met with trouble.

00:18:37.340 --> 00:18:39.260
So they're somewhere around here?

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:42.180
You need permission to
go anywhere but the park.

00:18:42.180 --> 00:18:43.180
But...

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:48.520
With a girl captive, they couldn't have taken a train very far.

00:18:48.520 --> 00:18:49.390
Yeah.

00:18:50.520 --> 00:18:53.150
Search everywhere near this station!

00:18:57.740 --> 00:18:58.820
Up we go!

00:19:08.160 --> 00:19:10.330
Let's check Shin-Shibaura, too.

00:19:35.610 --> 00:19:36.690
Kaori!

00:19:38.990 --> 00:19:40.860
We found her! We're in...

00:19:40.860 --> 00:19:43.370
Kaori, wake up!

00:19:47.870 --> 00:19:49.200
Kaori!

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:56.380
Come on. No point staying here.

00:19:56.380 --> 00:19:57.670
Can you stand?

00:19:58.170 --> 00:19:59.550
Careful, now.

00:19:59.550 --> 00:20:00.670
You brats!

00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:02.680
What do you think you're doing?

00:20:04.590 --> 00:20:06.390
Th-Those uniforms.

00:20:06.390 --> 00:20:07.600
You cops?

00:20:07.600 --> 00:20:10.850
Nope. We're from the Railway Public Security Force.

00:20:10.850 --> 00:20:13.230
Damn it. What are they doing here?

00:20:16.110 --> 00:20:18.530
Take Kaori and get out of here!

00:20:18.530 --> 00:20:19.690
Right.

00:20:19.690 --> 00:20:21.400
Wh-What about you, Takayama?

00:20:22.240 --> 00:20:24.200
I've got business to take care of.

00:20:24.200 --> 00:20:26.620
I'm deputy leader, after all.

00:20:29.830 --> 00:20:31.200
Bastards!

00:20:31.580 --> 00:20:32.620
Let's rumble!

00:20:32.620 --> 00:20:33.870
Takayama!

00:20:40.510 --> 00:20:45.220
The group captured was involved with black market drug trading.

00:20:46.390 --> 00:20:50.970
Ms. Kaori just happened upon one of their deals, so they took her.

00:20:50.970 --> 00:20:53.350
Looks like she only got
scuffed up a bit, though.

00:20:53.350 --> 00:20:55.020
That was good work.

00:20:55.020 --> 00:20:57.270
It's not entirely praiseworthy, really.

00:20:57.270 --> 00:20:59.230
Looks like you have an interesting team.

00:20:59.230 --> 00:21:00.610
Perhaps I do.

00:21:00.610 --> 00:21:02.150
You must be having fun.

00:21:02.150 --> 00:21:05.070
Yeah, I guess I do like them.

00:21:05.070 --> 00:21:07.620
Especially Takayama.

00:21:10.290 --> 00:21:12.830
Your friend gets discharged today, right?

00:21:13.410 --> 00:21:14.410
Yeah. She was admitted just to be safe, after all.

00:21:14.410 --> 00:21:17.420
We will be arriving in Tokyo soon.

00:21:17.420 --> 00:21:18.340
I'm just glad she's okay.

00:21:18.340 --> 00:21:19.590
Please beware opening doors.

00:21:19.590 --> 00:21:22.710
Yeah, and it's all thanks to you guys.

00:21:23.300 --> 00:21:24.760
Thanks so much.

00:21:25.180 --> 00:21:26.300
No need to thank me.

00:21:26.300 --> 00:21:29.140
We have now arrived in Tokyo.

00:21:29.140 --> 00:21:30.680
My, I was surprised, though.

00:21:30.680 --> 00:21:31.560
Why?

00:21:31.560 --> 00:21:33.680
You've really changed, Takayama.

00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:34.730
Huh?

00:21:35.560 --> 00:21:37.600
You were pretty cool back there.

00:21:41.440 --> 00:21:42.570
Takayama.

00:21:46.110 --> 00:21:47.530
Go get 'em.

00:21:59.750 --> 00:22:02.090
I'll see you around!

00:22:06.050 --> 00:22:07.470
See you.

00:23:40.730 --> 00:23:42.270
The Dancer express train!

00:23:42.270 --> 00:23:46.820
The Amagi Express, which uses
JNR 183 series limited express cars,

00:23:46.820 --> 00:23:51.610
and the Izu Line, which uses
JNR 153 series express-duty cars,

00:23:51.610 --> 00:23:56.080
were combined and upgraded to the new JNR 185 series limited express DC cars

00:23:56.080 --> 00:23:57.330
for this special express train.

00:23:57.330 --> 00:23:58.910
All right, all right already.

00:23:58.910 --> 00:24:01.750
Why don't you take a break and listen to me sing instead?

00:24:01.750 --> 00:24:04.830
Rail Wars, Episode Four: I Think I'm in Love.

00:24:05.290 --> 00:24:08.380
I know you were waiting for me!
Now, welcome to the Noa Kashima concert!
